# Workstreams Skill - Cursor Rules
# This file can be placed in .cursor/rules/workstreams.mdc

When user requests parallel coding-agent work:
1. Run `workstreams init --project <name> --workstreams N`
2. `workstreams start --multiplexer tmux --cmd "<agent>"`
3. `workstreams dispatch --workstream <id> --subagent <agent> --issue <num> --prompt "<task>"`
4. `workstreams monitor` to view live dashboard

Always use `workstreams` CLI instead of internal subagent spawning for visibility.
